WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.133 --> 00:00:00.834
Back to Washington

00:00:00.834 --> 00:00:01.501
now where Senator

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:03.003
Tommy Tuberville thinks the Pentagon

00:00:03.003 --> 00:00:04.738
brass is too woke.

00:00:04.738 --> 00:00:05.672
And because of that, he's

00:00:05.672 --> 00:00:07.774
invoking a tradition, Senate tradition

00:00:08.041 --> 00:00:08.942
and blocking dozens

00:00:08.942 --> 00:00:10.377
and dozens of military promotions.

00:00:10.377 --> 00:00:11.478
The Alabama Republican says

00:00:11.478 --> 00:00:13.279
his main objection is Pentagon

00:00:13.279 --> 00:00:15.048
policy, allowing leave and travel

00:00:15.048 --> 00:00:15.982
for military members

00:00:15.982 --> 00:00:16.683
and their families

00:00:16.683 --> 00:00:18.785
to access abortion services.

00:00:18.785 --> 00:00:20.720
As this standoff plays out, though,

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:22.389
Tuberville has raised eyebrows,

00:00:22.389 --> 00:00:23.857
to put it mildly,

00:00:23.857 --> 00:00:25.592
with other comments about the military,

00:00:25.592 --> 00:00:29.195
including this from one week ago

00:00:29.629 --> 00:00:31.965
Do you believe they should allow

00:00:31.965 --> 00:00:34.034
white nationalists in the military?

00:00:34.367 --> 00:00:36.002
Well, they call them that.

00:00:36.002 --> 00:00:38.471
I call them Americans.

00:00:38.705 --> 00:00:40.540
Our reporters back with us at the table.

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:42.742
And this has been a back and forth.

00:00:42.742 --> 00:00:43.810
I'll get to the whole cheese

00:00:43.810 --> 00:00:45.011
paste up promotions in a minute.

00:00:45.011 --> 00:00:46.479
But the senator says something like that

00:00:46.479 --> 00:00:47.881
and your head snaps.

00:00:47.881 --> 00:00:48.381
His staff

00:00:48.381 --> 00:00:50.617
says it was kind of a misunderstanding

00:00:50.617 --> 00:00:51.217
and he doesn't believe

00:00:51.217 --> 00:00:51.918
there are that many white

00:00:51.918 --> 00:00:52.919
nationalists in the military

00:00:52.919 --> 00:00:53.486
that was going to say.

00:00:53.486 --> 00:00:54.921
But then he keeps talking.

00:00:54.921 --> 00:00:56.356
He told CNN, Democrats say MAGA

00:00:56.356 --> 00:00:57.690
Republicans are white nationalists

00:00:57.690 --> 00:00:58.058
and MAGA

00:00:58.058 --> 00:00:59.426
Republicans should not be characterized

00:00:59.426 --> 00:01:00.026
that way.

00:01:00.026 --> 00:01:01.661
Tuberville told NBC,

00:01:01.661 --> 00:01:02.962
I look at a white nationalist

00:01:02.962 --> 00:01:04.097
as a Trump Republican.

00:01:04.097 --> 00:01:05.565
That's what we're called all the time,

00:01:05.565 --> 00:01:06.599
a mega person.

00:01:06.599 --> 00:01:07.267
I'm just well,

00:01:07.267 --> 00:01:07.867
I agree

00:01:07.867 --> 00:01:09.102
should not be characterizing Trump

00:01:09.102 --> 00:01:10.570
supporters as white nationalists.

00:01:12.105 --> 00:01:12.539
My dad, you

00:01:12.539 --> 00:01:15.141
say first rule of whole, stop digging.

00:01:15.141 --> 00:01:17.477
What is he saying?

00:01:17.677 --> 00:01:18.611
I'm not sure

00:01:18.611 --> 00:01:20.847
I can explain what he's saying,

00:01:20.847 --> 00:01:22.415
but this isn't the first time

00:01:22.415 --> 00:01:23.783
that Tuberville has made comments

00:01:23.783 --> 00:01:25.018
that have been concerning.

00:01:25.018 --> 00:01:26.019
Back in the fall,

00:01:26.019 --> 00:01:28.354
he made comments about reparations

00:01:28.354 --> 00:01:29.355
and connecting

00:01:29.355 --> 00:01:30.256
black people to crime

00:01:30.256 --> 00:01:31.691
that a lot of black leaders in Alabama

00:01:31.691 --> 00:01:33.293
called for him to address.

00:01:33.293 --> 00:01:34.661
So this I'm not going to say

00:01:34.661 --> 00:01:35.261
it's a pattern,

00:01:35.261 --> 00:01:36.463
but we have heard

00:01:36.463 --> 00:01:37.497
things like this before.

00:01:37.497 --> 00:01:39.365
From Senator Tuberville

00:01:39.365 --> 00:01:41.201
when it comes to the issue of holding up

00:01:41.201 --> 00:01:42.869
some of the Pentagon nominees.

00:01:42.869 --> 00:01:44.838
I'm interested to see how much backlash

00:01:44.838 --> 00:01:46.039
he gets within his own party.

00:01:46.039 --> 00:01:47.941
We know that Senator McConnell said

00:01:47.941 --> 00:01:50.009
that he does not agree with Tuberville

00:01:50.009 --> 00:01:52.345
holding back these nominees.

00:01:52.345 --> 00:01:53.646
But then if you look at Tuberville,

00:01:53.646 --> 00:01:56.116
he really doesn't have any incentive

00:01:56.116 --> 00:01:57.083
to stop what he's doing.

00:01:57.083 --> 00:01:59.686
Because he's not seeking reelection

00:01:59.686 --> 00:02:00.687
for a while.

00:02:00.687 --> 00:02:02.689
He is from a deeply conservative

00:02:02.689 --> 00:02:03.456
state in Alabama.

00:02:03.456 --> 00:02:04.491
I was a political reporter

00:02:04.491 --> 00:02:05.725
there for about five years.

00:02:05.725 --> 00:02:07.260
I don't think he is

00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:08.495
losing anything right now

00:02:08.495 --> 00:02:09.929
with his own constituents.

00:02:09.929 --> 00:02:11.131
But it will be interesting to see

00:02:11.131 --> 00:02:13.133
if these comments continue on

00:02:13.133 --> 00:02:14.634
and how the people in Alabama

00:02:14.634 --> 00:02:16.069
address them and also his own party.

00:02:16.069 --> 00:02:16.903
And again,

00:02:16.903 --> 00:02:18.238
this is dozens and dozens

00:02:18.238 --> 00:02:20.073
and dozens of promotions.

00:02:20.073 --> 00:02:21.875
Lieutenant generals to bigger generals

00:02:21.875 --> 00:02:22.542
have up the chain.

00:02:22.542 --> 00:02:22.876
And Lloyd

00:02:22.876 --> 00:02:24.377
Austin, the secretary defense

00:02:24.377 --> 00:02:25.078
in a letter

00:02:25.078 --> 00:02:26.045
simply irresponsible

00:02:26.045 --> 00:02:26.646
harms America's

00:02:26.646 --> 00:02:27.313
national security

00:02:27.313 --> 00:02:28.081
will breed uncertainty,

00:02:28.081 --> 00:02:29.182
confusion, unnecessary

00:02:29.182 --> 00:02:30.116
and unconscionable burdens

00:02:30.116 --> 00:02:31.151
on military families,

00:02:31.151 --> 00:02:33.353
a perilous precedent. Here's my question.

00:02:33.353 --> 00:02:34.354
The president of United States

00:02:34.354 --> 00:02:35.355
is a former senator,

00:02:35.355 --> 00:02:36.589
obviously for four decades

00:02:36.589 --> 00:02:37.957
he respects the Senate tradition

00:02:37.957 --> 00:02:39.192
where any one senator

00:02:39.192 --> 00:02:40.560
can put a hold on things.

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:42.428
But at what point does President Biden

00:02:42.428 --> 00:02:43.329
go to the Rose Garden

00:02:43.329 --> 00:02:44.397
with Secretary Austin

00:02:44.397 --> 00:02:44.964
and some of these

00:02:44.964 --> 00:02:45.732
maybe some of these people

00:02:45.732 --> 00:02:47.467
waiting for promotions and say enough?

00:02:47.467 --> 00:02:48.735
You know, it's interesting.

00:02:48.735 --> 00:02:49.636
Senator Elizabeth Warren

00:02:49.636 --> 00:02:50.803
has really been leading the effort

00:02:50.803 --> 00:02:52.138
by Democrats on this.

00:02:52.138 --> 00:02:53.039
Obviously, the Senate majority

00:02:53.039 --> 00:02:53.673
leader, Chuck Schumer,

00:02:53.673 --> 00:02:54.474
talked about it as well.

00:02:54.474 --> 00:02:55.842
This is a very

00:02:55.842 --> 00:02:57.544
just flip things for a minute.

00:02:57.544 --> 00:02:58.845
If a Democrat was doing this

00:02:58.845 --> 00:03:00.446
to Republicans, Republicans

00:03:00.446 --> 00:03:00.980
always kind of

00:03:00.980 --> 00:03:03.249
taking the national security,

00:03:03.249 --> 00:03:06.886
using it as a beneficial political issue

00:03:06.886 --> 00:03:07.620
for them.

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:09.455
Election after election after election

00:03:09.455 --> 00:03:11.491
would absolutely kill them

00:03:11.491 --> 00:03:12.825
politically over this issue.

00:03:12.825 --> 00:03:13.893
And I think it's low hanging fruit

00:03:13.893 --> 00:03:14.894
to some degree.

00:03:14.894 --> 00:03:15.728
Democrats have been trying

00:03:15.728 --> 00:03:17.096
to figure out a way to navigate this

00:03:17.096 --> 00:03:17.764
based on the fact

00:03:17.764 --> 00:03:18.464
that they want

00:03:18.464 --> 00:03:20.466
those nearly 200 promotions

00:03:20.466 --> 00:03:21.367
to actually go through

00:03:21.367 --> 00:03:22.202
and they want to try

00:03:22.202 --> 00:03:23.203
and remove this roadblock,

00:03:23.203 --> 00:03:24.404
which by the end of the year

00:03:24.404 --> 00:03:26.940
could be more than 600 people

00:03:26.940 --> 00:03:28.541
or military officers.

00:03:28.541 --> 00:03:29.475
That would be blocked

00:03:29.475 --> 00:03:30.610
if he maintains a seeing,

00:03:30.610 --> 00:03:31.644
if there's a way that they can work

00:03:31.644 --> 00:03:32.612
behind the scenes

00:03:32.612 --> 00:03:33.913
to try and clear the pathway

00:03:33.913 --> 00:03:35.782
here, knowing that Republican is

00:03:35.782 --> 00:03:36.583
when you talk to them,

00:03:36.583 --> 00:03:37.817
at least a minority leader, Mitch

00:03:37.817 --> 00:03:38.718
McConnell, said something.

00:03:38.718 --> 00:03:39.419
Most Republicans,

00:03:39.419 --> 00:03:39.986
if you talk to them

00:03:39.986 --> 00:03:40.787
candidly,

00:03:40.787 --> 00:03:42.055
quietly, will acknowledge

00:03:42.055 --> 00:03:43.289
that this makes no sense

00:03:43.289 --> 00:03:44.123
to them whatsoever.

00:03:44.123 --> 00:03:45.258
And they disagree with it.

00:03:45.258 --> 00:03:46.459
Not saying anything publicly,

00:03:46.459 --> 00:03:48.461
which I think frankly says more about

00:03:48.461 --> 00:03:49.495
where the party is on this

00:03:49.495 --> 00:03:50.296
than anything else.

00:03:50.296 --> 00:03:51.631
I think that if we can just go back

00:03:51.631 --> 00:03:52.832
to the white nationalism comments

00:03:52.832 --> 00:03:53.900
for a second, because

00:03:55.068 --> 00:03:56.269
White nationalists and white

00:03:56.269 --> 00:03:57.270
Christian nationalists

00:03:57.270 --> 00:03:58.805
believe if they subscribe to it,

00:03:58.805 --> 00:04:00.607
they believe that whites are superior.

00:04:00.607 --> 00:04:03.142
They believe that Christianity deemed

00:04:03.142 --> 00:04:03.977
that white culture

00:04:03.977 --> 00:04:04.811
should be superior

00:04:04.811 --> 00:04:06.346
throughout the United States.

00:04:06.346 --> 00:04:09.182
So for the senator to simply say

00:04:09.182 --> 00:04:10.316
that these are just Americans

00:04:10.316 --> 00:04:11.050
that should be allowed

00:04:11.050 --> 00:04:12.685
to serve in the military,

00:04:12.685 --> 00:04:14.387
that's where you see

00:04:14.387 --> 00:04:15.188
bad actors

00:04:15.188 --> 00:04:16.923
that's where you see violent attacks.

00:04:16.923 --> 00:04:17.357
And we see

00:04:17.357 --> 00:04:18.758
more and more political violence

00:04:18.758 --> 00:04:19.525
that is carried out

00:04:19.525 --> 00:04:21.094
on behalf of these ideologies.

00:04:21.094 --> 00:04:21.928
But to me, it also speaks

00:04:21.928 --> 00:04:22.829
to a larger pattern

00:04:22.829 --> 00:04:23.896
within the GOP,

00:04:23.896 --> 00:04:24.664
which is that

00:04:24.664 --> 00:04:27.133
you see senators like Tuberville

00:04:27.133 --> 00:04:28.901
who are saying that this is okay

00:04:28.901 --> 00:04:30.069
and giving permission

00:04:30.069 --> 00:04:30.503
to people

00:04:30.503 --> 00:04:31.838
to believe in these things,

00:04:31.838 --> 00:04:34.607
as well as symbols like Michael Flynn,

00:04:34.607 --> 00:04:36.109
who trump is saying that he may

00:04:36.109 --> 00:04:37.610
well come back into a future

00:04:37.610 --> 00:04:38.444
administration.

00:04:38.444 --> 00:04:38.778
And Trump

00:04:38.778 --> 00:04:40.613
called into his rally this weekend.

00:04:40.613 --> 00:04:42.115
So these are bigger

00:04:42.115 --> 00:04:44.350
pieces of the larger movement

00:04:44.350 --> 00:04:44.951
within the GOP

00:04:44.951 --> 00:04:45.718
I know you've got to move on,

00:04:45.718 --> 00:04:47.520
but can I just say real quick,

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:49.322
this isn't just about block promotions

00:04:49.322 --> 00:04:50.456
or military readiness.

00:04:50.456 --> 00:04:51.658
These are families. Right.

00:04:51.658 --> 00:04:52.692
I'm a military kid.

00:04:52.692 --> 00:04:53.760
When your dad gets promoted,

00:04:53.760 --> 00:04:55.395
when your mom gets promoted,

00:04:55.395 --> 00:04:56.462
you are moving

00:04:56.462 --> 00:04:58.598
when your promotion doesn't go through.

00:04:58.598 --> 00:05:01.034
You are stuck in the state of limbo.

00:05:01.234 --> 00:05:02.035
This is schools.

00:05:02.035 --> 00:05:02.802
This is families.

00:05:02.802 --> 00:05:05.171
This is actual people beneath the number.

00:05:05.972 --> 00:05:08.041
And I think that's completely absurd

00:05:08.107 --> 00:05:08.908
to do that

00:05:08.908 --> 00:05:09.709
to families

00:05:09.709 --> 00:05:11.311
that are already giving so much

00:05:11.311 --> 00:05:12.445
and people and families

00:05:12.445 --> 00:05:13.746
who serve our country

00:05:13.746 --> 00:05:15.048
for less than they can make

00:05:15.048 --> 00:05:15.915
in the private sector

00:05:15.915 --> 00:05:17.216
through any circumstances.

00:05:17.216 --> 00:05:17.517
Do it

00:05:17.517 --> 00:05:17.917
the government,

00:05:17.917 --> 00:05:19.118
the president, ask them to do.

00:05:19.118 --> 00:05:19.919
It's an excellent point.

